">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years back to 1951, and January to February came in under 90% of normal in 36 of them on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids. In 2025 on that middle, May to June hit 176% of normal while November to December fell to 46%. In 2026 so far, February to March sits at 55%. Every grid had its driest year in 2007, with grid 17568 at 59%.</p>"}
